import QOU.BringsSurface.BringReflectionParity
import QOU.BringsSurface.BringTripleSelection

/-!
# The exact discrete sunset on the Bring map graph

Bean `qou-u81q` (owner card 2026-11-28, "Both", with the orbifold signatures). This is a finite
model of the typed spectral sunset of `QOU/Transcendental/BringsSurface/BringSpectralSunset.lean`.
The Laplacian there is the hyperbolic one, whose eigenvalues are transcendental and not computed.
Here it is the combinatorial Laplacian `Δ = 4 I − Adj` of the vertex graph of the Bring map
`{5,4}`. Everything is an integer, and everything is checked by `decide +kernel`.

## The graph

The 30 vertices are the cosets `x ⟨S⟩` (`repV`, `cosets_distinct`); vertex `i` is joined to the
vertex of `rv i · S^k · A` for `k = 0, …, 3` (`nbrT`, `nbr_correct`). `S₅` acts on the left and
the reflection `c` by `x ↦ x T` (`actions_correct`, `class_actions_correct`).

## Results

* **Typed decomposition** (`projectors_sum`, `orth_k_l`, `projectors_equivariant`,
  `projectors_characters`). Seven equivariant projectors `P_k` (stored as `120 P_k`) with
  `Σ P_k = I` and `P_k P_l = δ_kl P_k`. On the image of `P_k` the traces of `g` and `g c` are
  `χ_{ρ_k}(g)` and `± χ_{ρ_k}(g)`. So
  `ℚ³⁰ = triv⁺ ⊕ std⁺ ⊕ [2,1,1,1]⁻ ⊕ [3,2]⁺ ⊕ [2,2,1]⁺ ⊕ [2,2,1]⁻ ⊕ [3,1,1]⁻`.
* **Spectrum** (`laplacian_on_types`, `graph_spectrum`). Each type has multiplicity one, so `Δ`
  is the scalar `λ = 0, 5, 7, 2, 6, 4, 2` on it. Hence `spec Δ = {0¹, 2¹¹, 4⁵, 5⁴, 6⁵, 7⁴}`,
  and the eigenvalue `2` carries two types.
* **Green function** (`green_function`). `G = Σ_{k ≠ triv} P_k / λ_k` satisfies
  `Δ G = I − J/30`.
* **Selection rule** (`sunset_selection`). The typed partial sunset
  `Σ_{x,y} G_a G_b G_c (x,y)` vanishes on every triple forbidden by
  `TripleSelection.allowedParity`.
* **Necessary, not sufficient** (`allowed_but_zero`). The allowed triple
  `std⁺ ⊗ std⁺ ⊗ [3,2]⁺` also gives zero.
* **The sunset** (`discrete_sunset`). `Σ_{x,y} G(x,y)³ = 18364201 / 22680000`.

The projector data are computed by `computations/probes/bring_discrete_sunset_probe.py`, and every
property used is checked here; nothing about them is assumed. Of the inputs, only the character
table is cited, and it is derived in `S5CharacterDerivation.lean`. No empirical value enters.
-/

namespace QOU.Brings.DiscreteSunset

